{
  "schema_version": 1,
  "id": "dragon-circling-phase-choice",
  "title": "Circling dragons choose landing at completed routes",
  "description": "Thirty-two separated dragons repeatedly finish orbit routes above their flight nodes. With no fight crystals, vanilla chooses landing with probability one third per eligible route decision. The creative observer must not become a strafe target. Aggregate threshold allows random route lengths and choices; it does not require identical random streams. Per-sample altitude/yaw resets run as one batch, preserving individual horizontal positions and keeping the fixture within the headless client lifetime.",
  "category": "entity",
  "tags": [
    "ender-dragon",
    "ai"
  ],
